-- title:
--   Index of nested 𝒪ᵥ-lattices equals inverse norm of determinant
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field and $v$ a height-one prime of its ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$, with $v$-adic completion $K_v$ (Lean: `v.adicCompletion K`) and valuation ring $\mathcal{O}_v$ (Lean: `v.adicCompletionIntegers K`). Let $V$ be an additive commutative group carrying compatible module structures over $K_v$ and over $\mathcal{O}_v$, the two being linked by a scalar-tower hypothesis, and let $\iota$ be a finite index type with decidable equality. Let $b_1, b_2 : \iota \to V$ be two $K_v$-bases of $V$, and assume that each $b_1(i)$ lies in the $\mathcal{O}_v$-submodule $\Lambda_2$ generated by the range of $b_2$. Writing $\Lambda_1$ for the $\mathcal{O}_v$-submodule generated by the range of $b_1$, the conclusion asserts that the relative index of the underlying additive subgroups, that is the index of $\Lambda_1$ inside $\Lambda_2$, regarded as a real number, multiplied by the norm $\lVert \det\nolimits_{b_2}(b_1) \rVert$ of the determinant in $K_v$ of the change-of-basis matrix expressing $b_1$ in the basis $b_2$, equals $1$. (Should the index be infinite, the relative index is $0$ by convention, so the equality also encodes its finiteness.)
--
--   This is the non-archimedean counterpart of the classical formula $[\Lambda_2:\Lambda_1] = \lvert\det\rvert$ for nested lattices in a real vector space, here with the normalised $v$-adic absolute value in place of the archimedean one. It is used in the adelic bookkeeping for automorphic forms, where indices of lattices under local change of basis must be compared with norms of determinants.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDedekindDomain_HeightOneSpectrum_relIndex_span_range_mul_norm_det_eq_one_of_forall_mem_span.lean

